meta {
  name: Sell
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/trade/sell/ACHR?quantity=1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  quantity: 1
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Manual Sell
  
  Places a manual market SELL for testing. Subject to the no-short guardrail —
  the quantity cannot exceed the tracked held quantity, so this can only
  flatten/reduce an existing long position, never open a short. Recorded in the
  trade log as strategy "MANUAL". Reduces or clears the tracked position on success.
  
  ## Path / Query
  - `{ticker}` — equity symbol, case-insensitive (e.g. AAPL)
  - `quantity` — shares to sell (default 1)
  
  ## Responses
  - `200` — { side, ticker, quantity, success, orderId, message, orderRequest,
    webullHttpStatus, webullResponse, submittedToWebull, mode, heldAfter, timestamp }
  - `422` — guardrail rejection (e.g. SHORT_BLOCKED when selling more than held)
  - `400` — invalid input (non-positive quantity)
  
  ## Debugging fields
  - `orderRequest` — the exact order payload we sent to Webull. Manual SELL uses
    order_type=MARKET. (Strategy bracket exits use STOP_LOSS / LIMIT with prices.)
  - `webullHttpStatus` — HTTP status from Webull (-1 = not sent / simulated / guardrail)
  - `webullResponse` — raw Webull success/failure body
  - `submittedToWebull` — true only when the order actually reached Webull
  
  ## Note
  Orders only reach Webull when webull.trading.submit-orders=true. POST places a
  REAL order in LIVE mode; sent to the sandbox in PAPER mode (with submit-orders).
}
